  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7dde1faf6ac8848188b51dc197e8f2fe, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SceneContextObject
  objectId: blacksmith_area
  displayName: The Forge
  objectType: Work Area
  description: Borin's forge, the practical work center of the village, where iron
    has been worked for as long as anyone remembers. Tools, locks, hinges, nails,
    and the metal fittings for carts and doors are made and mended here, and animals
    are shod at the door. The walls are dark with soot and the benches scarred by
    years of labor and old repairs. People bring things here to be weighed, measured,
    fixed, or proven, so plain physical facts count for far more than tavern rumor.
    Borin works the iron himself and trusts only what he can see and test.
  tags:
  - forge
  - blacksmith
  - metal
  - tools
  - locks
  - hinges
  - carts
  - repair
  - labor
  - evidence
  stateFacts:
  - Borin works the iron at the forge
  - Tools, locks, hinges, nails, and cart fittings are made and mended here
  - The forge has served the village for generations
  - Soot and worn benches show years of labor and repairs
  - Physical proof matters more here than rumor
  - Borin can judge whether something heavy could be moved
